Bootstrap CI loop must skip undefined diagnostics, not only infinite ones

_diagnostics_from_ingredients returns None whenever a ratio's denominator
is undefined: sdr and thi when a resample made no tool calls at all, err
when it produced no malformed calls to recover from, and every metric when
the resample is empty. Its docstring is explicit that None is returned
"instead of a zero or 1.0 that would visually flatter the model", so those
cells are meant to be excluded from the statistic rather than counted.

add_cis_to_diagnostics filters float("inf") but not None, so a None reaches
samples[m] and the subsequent vals.sort() raises

    TypeError: '<' not supported between instances of 'NoneType' and 'NoneType'

This fires on the shipped corpus with the documented reproduction command,
so `run_metrics.py results/ --subset paper_baseline` cannot complete as
released. It is reachable from both ends of the capability ladder: a model
good enough never to emit a malformed call leaves err undefined, and a model
too weak to emit any call leaves sdr and thi undefined.

--- a/harness/metrics.py
+++ b/harness/metrics.py
@@ -284,7 +284,7 @@
             d = _diagnostics_from_ingredients(sample)
             for m in _DIAG_METRICS:
                 v = d[m]
-                if v == float("inf"):
+                if v is None or v == float("inf"):
                     continue
                 samples[m].append(v)
         for m in _DIAG_METRICS:
